# Intent: A protected setup window (safety-and-privacy.md finding 4). A new six-digit setup code is made each time setup opens and shown on the unit's screen after the hotspot name; /submit refuses anything without it, in constant time, and five wrong codes lock the window. The window ends after 8 minutes (the unit then starts a new one with a new code). The hotspot name is generic: MaiPai-StackChan-<last four hex of the Wi-Fi address>. The screen hint is let through when captions are off, because captions off silenced it (F02) and nobody could read the code. The code is wiped when setup stops.
# Placement: unit (the code lives in RAM and on the unit's screen only; a neighbour cannot see it)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc of the StackChan tree (MIT); firmware/portal/maipai_wifi_configuration_ap.cc from P02
# Check after a flash: none until P05 turns it on
